  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday night through next Sunday)\nIssued at 1031 PM CDT Sun Aug 23 2026\n\nLuckily, Monday will be the hottest day of the week and Tuesday will \nbe the start of a \"cool\" down the rest of the week. The upper \nridging that parked over the region the past few days will finally \nbegin to retreat west on Tuesday. Models are in agreement the upper \nridging will remain over the Desert Southwest through the latter \nhalf of the week. Although Tuesday will be slightly cooler compared \nto Monday, high temperatures will remain in the triple digits. Highs \noff the Caprock will be around Heat Advisory temperatures(105-109 \ndegrees), therefore can expect a Heat Advisory issued in future \nforecasts. High temperatures the rest of the week will range from \nmid 90s to just below Heat Advisory temperatures. Multiple passing \nembedded shortwaves will bring thunderstorm chances every late \nafternoon and evening from Tuesday through Thursday. Sadly, models \nare indicating the upper ridging will push back east over the region \nthrough the weekend bringing dry conditions and very hot \ntemperatures again.",
